--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Thai Character Cluster grammar -- src/unsegbench/clusters.py
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The regular-expression grammar in `_RE_TCC` / `TCC_PATTERN` is ported from
PyThaiNLP (`pythainlp.tokenize.tcc`), which is licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0. PyThaiNLP derives it in turn from Wittawat Jitkrittum's `jtcc`
(TCC.g), implementing the Thai Character Cluster rules of:

    Theeramunkong, T., Sornlertlamvanich, V., Tanhermhong, T., Chinnan, W.
    (2000). Character Cluster Based Thai Information Retrieval.
    Proceedings of the Fifth International Workshop on Information Retrieval
    with Asian Languages.

    SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2016-2026 PyThaiNLP Project
    SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

A copy of the Apache License, Version 2.0 is available at:

    http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

The grammar is vendored rather than imported so that the core package works
without optional dependencies. It is cross-checked against the PyThaiNLP
reference implementation in the test suite.

